    "coreConcept": "Path normalization and resolution, atomic filesystem operations via Files, and memory-efficient lazy line streaming with Files.lines()",
    "timeComplexity": "O(1) atomic filesystem operations, O(N) line stream",
    "spaceComplexity": "O(1) lazy heap memory buffer",
    "description": "Mastering modern NIO.2 filesystem mechanics: Path operations, atomic file operations, attribute inspection, and lazy line streaming.",
    "theory": "# Module 15: NIO.2 File System \u2014 Paths, Files API CRUD & Memory-Efficient Streaming\n\n> **Source Track:** Oracle Java Tutorials \u2014 *Essential Java Classes*  \n> **Source Lessons:** `io/fileio.html`, `path.html`, `pathClass.html`, `fileOps.html`, `check.html`, `delete.html`, `copy.html`, `move.html`, `fileAttr.html`, `file.html`  \n> **Scope:** `java.nio.file.Path`, `java.nio.file.Files`, Atomic Operations, File Attributes (`BasicFileAttributes`), Memory-Efficient Lazy Streaming (`Files.lines()`).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Architectural Overview: The NIO.2 Filesystem API\n\nIntroduced in Java 7 (`java.nio.file`), NIO.2 completely replaces the legacy `java.io.File` with an extensible, high-performance filesystem abstraction:\n- **`Path`:** A platform-independent hierarchical locator representing a file or directory path.\n- **`Files`:** A rich utility class consisting exclusively of static methods operating on `Path` instances.\n- **Atomic File Operations:** Direct support for atomic moves and symbolic links.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    Path[\"java.nio.file.Path (Platform-independent locator)\"]\n    Files[\"java.nio.file.Files Static Utilities\"]\n    Ops[\"File CRUD, Atomic Move, Attributes, Lazy Line Streaming\"]\n\n    Path --> Files --> Ops\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Path Operations: Resolve, Relativize & Normalize\n\n- **Resolve (Concatenation):** `basePath.resolve(\"sub/file.txt\")` joins path segments.\n- **Relativize:** `pathA.relativize(pathB)` calculates the relative navigation needed to reach `pathB` from `pathA`.\n- **Normalize:** `path.normalize()` eliminates redundant `.` and `..` tokens.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Exhaustive Member Function & Files Reference\n\n| Category | Method / Syntax (Example) | Use Case (Code Snippet) | Complexity | Description & Behavioral Invariant |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Path Builder** | `Path.of(\"a\", \"b\")` | `Path p = Path.of(\"var\", \"logs\", \"app.log\");` | $O(1)$ object build | Constructs platform-independent path. |\n| **Check Exists** | `Files.exists(path)` | `if (Files.exists(p) && Files.isRegularFile(p))`| Native OS stat | Verifies existence without following symlinks if specified. |\n| **Atomic Move** | `Files.move(s, d, opt)`| `Files.move(src, dst, StandardCopyOption.ATOMIC_MOVE);`| Native rename | Performs atomic filesystem rename. |\n| **Create Directories**| `Files.createDirectories(p)`| `Files.createDirectories(targetDir);` | $O(D)$ mkdir -p | Recursively creates all non-existent parent directories. |\n| **Lazy Lines Stream** | `Files.lines(path)` | `try (Stream<String> s = Files.lines(p)) { ... }`| $O(1)$ lazy memory | Streams lines lazily from disk without buffering entire file in heap. |\n| **Write String** | `Files.writeString(p, s)`| `Files.writeString(p, data, StandardOpenOption.CREATE);`| $O(N)$ write | Convenient Java 11+ utility for writing text files via UTF-8. |\n\n---\n\n## 4. Modern Idiomatic Java Code Implementation\n\n```java\n// Comprehensive demonstration of NIO.2 Path operations, atomic moves, and lazy line streaming\npackage devtype.engine.io;\n\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.nio.file.*;\nimport java.util.stream.Stream;\n\npublic final class ModernNioLab {\n\n    public static long countErrorOccurrences(Path logPath, String keyword) throws IOException {\n        // Memory-efficient lazy line streaming\n        try (Stream<String> lines = Files.lines(logPath)) {\n            return lines.filter(line -> line.contains(keyword)).count();\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void saveConfigSafely(Path targetFile, String data) throws IOException {\n        Path tempFile = Files.createTempFile(targetFile.getParent(), \"cfg-\", \".tmp\");\n        Files.writeString(tempFile, data, StandardOpenOption.TRUNCATE_EXISTING);\n        // Atomic filesystem rename replaces target cleanly\n        Files.move(tempFile, targetFile, StandardCopyOption.ATOMIC_MOVE, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING);\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 5. Common Traps, Anti-Patterns & Best Practices\n\n1. **Leaking File Descriptors with `Files.lines()`:**\n   - *Trap:* Invoking `Files.lines(path)` without wrapping it in a try-with-resources statement leaves the underlying file descriptor open.\n   - *Remedy:* Always use `try (Stream<String> lines = Files.lines(path))`.",
    "code": "package devtype.engine.io;\n\nimport java.io.IOException;\nimport java.nio.file.*;\nimport java.util.stream.Stream;\n\npublic final class ModernNioLab {\n\n    public static long countErrorOccurrences(Path logPath, String keyword) throws IOException {\n        try (Stream<String> lines = Files.lines(logPath)) {\n            return lines.filter(line -> line.contains(keyword)).count();\n        }\n    }\n\n    public static void saveConfigSafely(Path targetFile, String data) throws IOException {\n        Path tempFile = Files.createTempFile(targetFile.getParent(), \"cfg-\", \".tmp\");\n        Files.writeString(tempFile, data, StandardOpenOption.TRUNCATE_EXISTING);\n        Files.move(tempFile, targetFile, StandardCopyOption.ATOMIC_MOVE, StandardCopyOption.REPLACE_EXISTING);\n    }\n}"
