    "description": "Externalizing application configuration: Properties persistence, XML streams, cascading fallback hierarchies, and CLI arguments.",
    "theory": "# Module 20: Platform Environment I \u2014 Properties Persistence, XML Streams & CLI Parsing\n\n> **Source Track:** Oracle Java Tutorials \u2014 *Essential Java Classes*  \n> **Source Lessons:** `environment/config.html`, `properties.html`, `cmdLineArgs.html`, `env.html`, `other.html`  \n> **Scope:** `java.util.Properties` Table Persistence, `.properties` & XML Streams, Default Properties Hierarchies, CLI Argument Parsing (`String[] args`), Environment Variables (`System.getenv()`).\n\n---\n\n## 1. Architectural Overview & Configuration Hierarchy\n\nExternal configuration allows application behavior to be customized across staging, test, and production environments without recompilation. Java establishes a clear hierarchy:\n1. **Command-Line Arguments (`String[] args`):** Highest priority runtime overrides.\n2. **System Properties (`-Dkey=value`):** Process-wide JVM properties.\n3. **Environment Variables (`System.getenv()`):** OS shell environment settings.\n4. **Properties Files (`.properties`):** Persistent configuration files on disk.\n\n```mermaid\nflowchart TD\n    File[\"config.properties on Disk\"] -->|\"props.load(InputStream)\"| Props[\"Properties Map in Memory\"]\n    Props -->|\"getProperty('db.port', '5432')\"| Value[\"'5432' (Fallback Default)\"]\n```\n\n---\n\n## 2. Exhaustive Member Function & Properties Reference\n\n| Category | Method / Syntax (Example) | Use Case (Code Snippet) | Complexity | Description & Behavioral Invariant |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Load Properties** | `props.load(stream)` | `props.load(Files.newInputStream(path));` | O(Lines) parse | Parses `.properties` stream; handles escapes. |\n| **Get Property** | `props.getProperty(k, def)`| `String port = props.getProperty(\"port\", \"8080\");`| O(1) hash read | Reads configuration value with default fallback. |\n| **Store Properties**| `props.store(out, comment)`| `props.store(out, \"Application Config\");`| O(N) stream write | Serializes properties map to text file with timestamp. |\n| **Read Env** | `System.getenv(\"KEY\")` | `String path = System.getenv(\"PATH\");` | O(1) read | Reads environment variable from parent OS shell. |\n\n---\n\n## 3. Modern Idiomatic Java Code Implementation\n\n```java\n// Comprehensive demonstration of Properties loading and fallback hierarchy\npackage devtype.engine.platform;\n\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.nio.file.Files;\nimport java.nio.file.Path;\nimport java.util.Properties;\n\npublic final class PropertiesConfigLab {\n\n    public static Properties loadConfig(Path configPath) throws IOException {\n        Properties defaults = new Properties();\n        defaults.setProperty(\"server.port\", \"8080\");\n        defaults.setProperty(\"timeout.ms\", \"5000\");\n\n        Properties appProps = new Properties(defaults); // Fallback hierarchy\n        if (Files.exists(configPath)) {\n            try (InputStream in = Files.newInputStream(configPath)) {\n                appProps.load(in);\n            }\n        }\n        return appProps;\n    }\n}\n```\n\n---\n\n## 4. Common Traps, Anti-Patterns & Best Practices\n\n1. **Attempting to Mutate `System.getenv()`:**\n   - *Trap:* `System.getenv()` returns an unmodifiable read-only map; calling `put()` throws `UnsupportedOperationException`.\n   - *Remedy:* Use `System.setProperty()` for runtime configuration mutation.",
    "code": "package devtype.engine.platform;\n\nimport java.io.*;\nimport java.nio.file.Files;\nimport java.nio.file.Path;\nimport java.util.Properties;\n\npublic final class PropertiesConfigLab {\n\n    public static Properties loadConfig(Path configPath) throws IOException {\n        Properties defaults = new Properties();\n        defaults.setProperty(\"server.port\", \"8080\");\n        defaults.setProperty(\"timeout.ms\", \"5000\");\n\n        Properties appProps = new Properties(defaults); // Fallback hierarchy\n        if (Files.exists(configPath)) {\n            try (InputStream in = Files.newInputStream(configPath)) {\n                appProps.load(in);\n            }\n        }\n        return appProps;\n    }\n}"
